#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Eight-node Yellowback v3 regtest for YecWallet, ARMED when `up` returns.

Node 0 is the funded wallet, node 1 is stock, nodes 2-4 are signalling pools
with fixed payout addresses, and nodes 5-7 are attestor nodes (enforcing, no
payout). Pool quotes go in with yed_setquote, either directly from this script
(the default) or, with `up --agents`, through one real `yellowback-quote
--mock-price` process per pool -- the same path a pool runs.

Each attestor node registers itself with yed_registerattestor (10 YEC, 200
blocks), `up` mines through BOND_MATURITY and ATTEST_ARM_DELAY, and the devnet
ends ARMED. One real `yellowback-attest attest --mock-price` runs beside each
attestor node and one `yellowback-attest subscribe` beside node 0, both on the
`dir` transport -- no relay, no network. `--no-attest` gives back the five-node
v2 devnet. No federation, coordinators, anchors, rosters or endpoints.

YELLOWBACK_DEVNET_DIR and YELLOWBACK_DEVNET_PORTSEED (or PORTBASE) let two
devnets run side by side.

Commands: up [--agents] [--no-attest], check, status, mine N [node],
price USD, attestor N {stop|start|price USD}, notice VAULTTXID, wallet,
cli [--node N | --datadir N] [-- args], down [--wipe].
"""
